# Naming

## Files and folders

- Files and folders: `kebab-case` (`order-details-page.tsx`, `filter-content/`).
- Extra kind in the filename uses a hyphen: `returns-types.ts`, `login-form-schema.ts`, `orders-store.ts`. Do not use `name.kind.ts`.
- Tool-required dotted suffixes stay: `.test.ts(x)`, `.module.scss`, `.d.ts`.
- SCSS: `<component-name>.module.scss` next to the `.tsx` of the same name. Never `style.module.scss` or `page.module.scss`.
- Two styled components in one directory → each gets its own folder.

## Code identifiers

- Components: `PascalCase` (`ExchangeDetailsHeader`).
- Hooks: `useSomething` (`useExchangeDetails`, `useDebouncedSearchQuery`).
- Booleans: `is` / `has` / `can` / `should` prefix (`isLoading`, `hasError`, `canCancel`).
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` (`SEARCH_DEBOUNCE_MS`, `DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE`).
- Types: `PascalCase` (`ExchangeDetails`, `CancelExchangePayload`).
- Callback props: `onX` (`onClose`, `onConfirm`, `onFiltersChange`).
- Local event handlers: `handleX` (`handleClose`, `handleConfirm`, `handleFiltersChange`).
- Collections: plural nouns (`orders`, `exchangeItems`, `visibleFilters`).
- Module public API: `index.ts` barrel. Import the folder/module barrel, not a file deep inside it.
- Avoid abbreviations unless domain-standard (`KZ`, `DTO`, `API`).

## Props and domain names

- Use precise domain names instead of vague ones: `exchange`, `buyer`, `waybill` — not `data`, `item`, `value`, `temp`.
- Query keys live in `query-keys.ts` and use a module prefix: `exchangeKeys.details(id)`.
- Zustand stores: `<domain>-store.ts` with a named hook export (`useExchangeFiltersStore`).

---

## Examples

### 1. File and folder names

```
# ❌ BAD
src/modules/exchange/components/ExchangeDetailsHeader.tsx
src/modules/exchange/components/exchangeDetails/style.module.scss
src/modules/exchange/api/exchange.types.ts

# ✅ GOOD
src/modules/exchange/components/exchange-details/exchange-details-header.tsx
src/modules/exchange/components/exchange-details/exchange-details-header.module.scss
src/modules/exchange/model/exchange-types.ts
```

### 2. Component and hook names

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
function exchangeHeader() { /* ... */ }
function getData() { /* ... */ }
function Exchange_details() { /* ... */ }

// ✅ GOOD
function ExchangeDetailsHeader() { /* ... */ }
function useExchangeDetails(exchangeId: string) { /* ... */ }
function mapExchangeToTimelineSteps(exchange: ExchangeDetails) { /* ... */ }
```

### 3. Boolean and handler names

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
type Props = {
  loading: boolean;
  disabled: boolean;
  click: () => void;
};

function ExchangeTabs({ loading, click }: Props) {
  const submit = () => click();
}

// ✅ GOOD
type Props = {
  isLoading: boolean;
  isDisabled: boolean;
  onTabChange: (tab: ExchangeTab) => void;
};

function ExchangeTabs({ isLoading, onTabChange }: Props) {
  const handleTabChange = (tab: ExchangeTab) => onTabChange(tab);
}
```

### 4. Types and constants

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
type data = { id: string; status: string };
const debounce = 300;
const ExchangeStatus = 'pending';

// ✅ GOOD
type ExchangeListItem = { id: string; status: ExchangeStatus };
const SEARCH_DEBOUNCE_MS = 300;
const EXCHANGE_TAB_TO_SHIP = 'to-ship' as const;
```

### 5. Import paths and barrels

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
import { ExchangeTimelineStep } from '@/modules/exchange/components/exchange-details/exchange-timeline-step';
import { useOrders } from '@/shared/api/order';

// ✅ GOOD
import { ExchangeDetailsPage } from '@/modules/exchange';
import { useExchangeDetails } from '@/modules/exchange/api/hooks'; // only inside the same module
import { Pagination } from '@/shared/ui';
```
